      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes Requested** — Missing test coverage for driver error paths.\n\n### Review Summary\n\n*   **Functionality:** ✅ The new test cases correctly simulate failures by injecting states into the mock SPI variables. \n*   **Architecture \u0026 Component Fit:** ✅ The tests integrate cleanly with the existing Zephyr `ZTEST` suite and correctly leverage the `fake_flash_ex_op` driver mock.\n*   **Code Simplicity:** ✅ Test control flow is minimal and clean.\n*   **Idiomaticity \u0026 Readability:** ✅ The tests use standard `ztest` conventions correctly.\n*   **Security:** ✅ N/A (test additions only).\n*   **Testing:** ❌ The `all\u003dtrue` failure path was successfully added to `test_status_register_write_failure`, but the test for the `prot_start !\u003d FLASH_PROTECTION_START` path in `cros_flash_rtkfp_get_protect_flags()` is still missing despite being marked as \"Done\". See inline comment.\n*   **CL Size \u0026 Scope:** ✅ `Size: S (+41, -0)`. The CL contains a single logical change: adding tests for the protection error mappings.\n*   **Commit Message:** ✅ The description clearly identifies the specific driver and error paths being tested. \n\n[[trajectory](https://goto.corp.google.com/traj/d2ae2cde-3d40-4b08-b753-be2adacbf0c3)]",
