      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] \nThis test case correctly covers `SRP0` and `SRP1` inconsistency, but there is still one more error path in `cros_flash_rtkfp_get_protect_flags()` that lacks test coverage (which I flagged on the previous patchset): when `spi_flash_reg_to_protect()` succeeds but `prot_start !\u003d FLASH_PROTECTION_START` (e.g. top-down protection with `TB\u003d0`), the driver returns `EC_FLASH_PROTECT_ERROR_INCONSISTENT`. \n\nEven though this was marked \"Done\" on Gerrit, the test case is not present in the current patchset. Please add it to cover this boundary condition:\n\n```c\nZTEST_USER(cros_flash_rtkfp, test_protect_flags_inconsistent_start)\n{\n\t/* Assuming TB\u003d0 (default), setting BP0 protects the top of the flash, \n\t * which sets prot_start !\u003d FLASH_PROTECTION_START (0).\n\t */\n\tfake_sr1 |\u003d SPI_FLASH_SR1_BP0;\n\n\tzassert_equal(cros_flash_physical_get_protect_flags(cros_flash_dev),\n\t\t      EC_FLASH_PROTECT_ERROR_INCONSISTENT);\n}\n```\n[🔗](http://go/tj/d2ae2cde-3d40-4b08-b753-be2adacbf0c3)",
